Experiment: include _FLOAT members in the integer UBWC compat classes.

Why. Stock keeps every _FLOAT out of fd6_ubwc_compat_mode(), and for R32_FLOAT
it says directly "a630 blob allows these, but not a660". a660 is our gen2
family, so the decision is deliberate, not an oversight. But because of it any format
list in which _SFLOAT is mixed with integers fails
tu6_mutable_format_list_ubwc_compatible() and loses compression entirely.

That is exactly how the five vkd3d classes are built, i.e. precisely what D3D12 builds for
TYPELESS resources (R32_TYPELESS, R16G16_TYPELESS, R32G32_TYPELESS,
R16G16B16A16_TYPELESS, R32G32B32A32_TYPELESS). Out of the 70 vkd3d classes on stock
31 classes keep UBWC, the other 39 lose it; this patch raises 31 -> 36.

Justification by layouts, not by blob. UBWC encoding is defined for a format
class, not for a concrete format, and within one class only
the channel sizes differ. An _SFLOAT member has exactly the same layout as the integer
member of the same typeless format: the same bits per channel, the same swizzle, the same
tiled markup. A cast in Vulkan is a reinterpretation of the same bits, not a
channel permutation, so fast-clear and sector decoding cannot
diverge. Z32_FLOAT deliberately stays UNKNOWN: it is not part of any
colour typeless family, and depth has its own clear semantics.

What this patch does not verify (and the risk that remains): the driver does not check
the contents of the UBWC fast-clear metadata against the format interpretation, so
a wrong clear value may show up only where the application does a
fast-clear through a view in a float interpretation. A byte roundtrip does not
catch it.

Measurement on Adreno 740 (chip_id 0x43050a01), probes U in
tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c, for the five TYPELESS classes:

  stock (0004-0006): list=0x100000 vs nonmut=0x102000   -> the list dropped UBWC
  with the patch:    list=0x102000                       -> the list kept it

  roundtrip (CopyBufferToImage -> CopyImageToBuffer, byte comparison):
  stock  linear/nonmut/list  0/262144, 0/262144, 0/262144    EXACT
  patch  linear/nonmut/list  0/262144, 0/262144, 0/262144    EXACT

No regressions: probes S (0005) and T (0006) still PASS.

